WEBVTT

00:28:57.958 --> 00:29:00.018
or is the effect stronger in reverse?"

00:29:00.042 --> 00:29:02.726
I can design those experiments
and try to adjudicate it.

00:29:02.750 --> 00:29:04.018
Would it convince you?

00:29:04.042 --> 00:29:07.726
EP: Yeah, but I think developmentally
in those moments, right?

00:29:07.750 --> 00:29:10.768
Because I think that one
of the best places to go look

00:29:10.792 --> 00:29:12.434
at how these things get layered,

00:29:12.458 --> 00:29:14.143
is to look at child development.

00:29:14.167 --> 00:29:15.434
So child development,

00:29:15.458 --> 00:29:17.893
the kid sits on your lap
and if all goes well,

00:29:17.917 --> 00:29:21.143
they are secure, they are nested,
they're safe, they trust.

00:29:21.167 --> 00:29:23.768
And it is from that place
that they jump into the world

00:29:23.792 --> 00:29:26.226
and they go, and they go
to explore and to discover

00:29:26.250 --> 00:29:28.351
and take risks and do their thing.

00:29:28.375 --> 00:29:31.893
Then they turn around,
and they ascertain if you're still there.